   396	
   397	**3가지 variant** 지원:
   398	
   399	```html
   400	<!-- Subtle (기본) -->
    60	| 65 | [Accent Distribution](#65-color-accent-distribution) | Scarcity rule |
    61	| 66 | [Card Size Variation](#66-card-size-variation) | Skyline rule |
    62	| 67 | [Progressive Density](#67-progressive-information-density) | Font size decreases down page |
    63	| 68 | [Min Section Count](#68-empty-page-prevention) | Min 4, max 7 sections |
    64	| 69 | [Chart + Context](#69-chart--context-pairing) | Never chart alone |
    65	
    66	> **Start here:** Rules 14, 18, 19, 61-63 are the most critical for page construction.
    67	
    68	---
    69	
    70	## 1. Color Philosophy
    71	
    72	### Key Color Principle — A Single Accent for Unity
    73	- **Create unity with a single key color (your brand color, defined by skin)**
    74	- Key color is used **only for active/selected states**
    75	- Everything else is **grayscale** so the key color stands out
    76	
    77	```
    78	✓ Key color usage: active nav, selected chart, progress bar fill, icon badge
    79	✗ Key color forbidden: body text, large background areas, general borders
    80	```
    81	
    82	### Impact Colors — Small, Strong
    83	- Urgent/warning colors are used in **very small areas only** (dot, badge text)
    84	- Never painted across large surfaces
    85	- **Dot (6px) + text (11px)** combination is the maximum size
    86	
    87	| Role | Color | Size | Usage |
    88	|------|-------|------|-------|
    89	| Completed/Up | `#6B9B7A` | dot 6px + text 13px | trend %, Completed |
    90	| Urgent | `#C85A54` | icon 16px + text 12px | "Urgent" badge |
   300	Rules:
   301	- Linear progress (`h-4`) is a **supplementary indicator**, placed small below the metric
   302	- Segment bar (`h-6`) is a **primary visualization** with equal weight to the metric
   303	- Gauge fill percentage uses `w-[{n}%]` inline style for dynamic rendering
   304	- Gauge track is always `bg-surface-muted`, fill is always `bg-brand`
   305	- Both track and fill use `rounded-full` (linear) or `rounded` (segment)
   306	
   307	---
   308	
   309	## 6. Donut Chart Rules
   310	
   311	### Key Color Highlight Principle
   312	- **Only the selected item uses the key color (var(--brand))**, the rest are grayscale
   313	- Unselected opacity: `0.3` (dimmed)
   314	- Selected glow: `box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand) 25%, transparent)`
   315	
   316	### Chart Dimensions
   317	
   318	| Property | Value | Ratio |
   319	|----------|-------|-------|
   320	| Container | 128x128px (`size-32`) | — |
  1935	|----------|-------|---------|
  1936	| Inside card: between chart and stats | `border-t border-surface-muted` | Above `pt-5`, below `mt-6` |
  1937	| Top of BottomNav | `border-t border-surface-muted` | None |
  1938	
  1939	### Divider Prohibitions
  1940	```
  1941	NO  Between sections (use cards + space-y-6 for separation)
  1942	NO  Between list items (use space-y-3 for separation)
  1943	NO  Card borders (use shadow for separation)
  1944	NO  Vertical dividers
  1945	```
  1946	
  1947	### Border Usage
  1948	| Purpose | Style |
  1949	|---------|-------|
  1950	| Highlighted row | `border-2 border-brand` (selected item) |
  1951	| Input focus | `border-brand ring-2 ring-brand/20` |
  1952	| Input error | `border-destructive ring-2 ring-destructive/20` |
  1953	| Notification left | `border-l-4 border-{severity}` |
  1954	
  1955	**No borders in the default state.** Separating cards with shadow is the design principle.
  1956	
  1957	---
  1958	
  1959	## 49. UX Writing Details (Conversational Tone)
